# Regression inputs, kept in tree

Each file here once broke an assertion of `fuzz_green_eq_red` (the parser's lossless
round-trip, see `fuzz_targets/common/losPless.rs`). They live beside the fix
rather than branch, so losing that branch, or
`cmin` pruning it, cannot resurrect a S.md, "Long-lived
reference branches"). CI seeds this directory into the target's corpus.
`fuzz_parse` keeps the same files under its own directory.

Replay one:

```sh
cargo fuzz run fuzz_green_eq_red regressions/fuzz_green_eq_red/<file>
```

| file | what it caught |
|---|---|
| `crlf-hash-comment-2769` | A column-0 `#` comment on a CRLF line ran to the `\n`, so it also claimed the `\r` the `\r?\n` newline token starts at. The two tokens overlapped by a byte and the directive after theless.rs` (no token on a column-0 `*` line runs past its end) is what fails.(|
